# Commit Message Template
#
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Types:
#   feat      → A new feature
#   fix       → A bug fix
#   docs      → Documentation changes
#   style     → Code style changes (formatting, semicolons, etc.)
#   refactor  → Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf      → A performance improvement
#   test      → Adding or updating tests
#   build     → Changes that affect the build system or dependencies
#   ci        → Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore     → Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#   revert    → Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scope: Optional. The section of the codebase affected (e.g., worker, api, ui).
#
# Subject: A short, imperative description of the change.
#
# Body: Optional. Detailed explanation of the change.
#
# Footer: Optional. Issue references (e.g., Closes #123, BREAKING CHANGE).
#
# Examples:
#   feat(worker): add Gemini AI response handling
#   fix(api): resolve webhook payload parsing error
#   docs(readme): update setup instructions
#   test: add unit tests for Telegram webhook handler
#   chore(deps): update wrangler to v4.92

# ---
# Do not modify lines starting with '#'.
# The first line is the commit subject, keep it under 72 characters.
# Separate the subject from body with a blank line.
# Wrap the body at 72 characters.
# ---
